summary: Test time backward for clock_gettime()
description: |
   This test reads clock_gettime rapidly and compares the results.  If
   clock_gettime returns decreasing values, ie time went backwards, then
   return an error
    Test input:
        Input details:
        - gtod_backwards.c, source.
    Expected results:
      The runtest script compiles and runs the test gtod_backwards for 1,000 iterations.
      The test returns an error if any one iteration fails.
      The runtime of the gtod_backwards test will be monitored, with a
      warning if it exceeds 480 minutes.
         Output details:
            "Time test Passed: "
            "rstrnt-report-result general/time/clock_gettime PASS 0"
    Results location:
        output.txt
contact: Qiao Zhao <qzhao@redhat.com>
id: 9603fdff-19d4-4552-9808-60a63de1fd07
component:
  - kernel
path: /general/time/clock_gettime
test: bash -x ./runtest.sh
framework: shell
duration: 1h
require:
